# File: tests/features/usage-with-claude.feature
# Generated from: specs/44-list-claude-s-usage-alongside-the-logged-in-providers-in-usage/requirements.md
Feature: List Claude's usage alongside the logged-in providers in /usage

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Claude's usage is listed with the providers'
    Given Claude's five_hour window is 23.5% used and its seven_day window 41%, and OpenCode Go has a stored login with a usage reading
    When the person runs /usage
    Then after the built-in command, the rows read "Plan usage", then "Claude" with "5h 24%" and "7d 41%", then "OpenCode Go" with its windows

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Claude with no reading
    Given Claude's usage has no rate-limit windows and OpenCode Go has a stored login
    When the person runs /usage
    Then the Claude entry reads "No usage reading available" and the OpenCode Go entry is unchanged

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: No provider login adds nothing
    Given no login-requiring provider has a stored login
    When the person runs /usage
    Then nmg-router adds no rows and the built-in command's result passes through unchanged
